SIGNAL MESSENGER, LLC

signal-edge implements the Signal protocol and Signal's service APIs by following, and in places
porting, Signal's own AGPL-3.0-only software. Copyright Signal Messenger, LLC.

- Signal-Desktop (https://github.com/signalapp/Signal-Desktop): device linking and provisioning,
  account and prekey management, the receive loop, sending (padding, device-list repair, sync
  transcripts, sender keys, sealed sender), retry requests, the storage service, groups, attachments,
  timers, mentions, quotes and reactions. Source files name the Desktop functions they follow. The
  sealed-sender trust roots and the zkgroup server public parameters are from its
  config/production.json.
- libsignal (https://github.com/signalapp/libsignal): sealed/ is built on its libsignal-protocol,
  zkgroup, libsignal-core and libsignal-account-keys crates (tag v0.106.1), so the prebuilt
  src/vendor/signal-sealed WebAssembly contains them. tls/res/ holds Signal's two root certificates
  from its rust/net/res/. Wire formats follow its protobuf definitions and its chat client.
- Signal-Android (https://github.com/signalapp/Signal-Android): referenced for how the apps treat
  disappearing-message timers.

